From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:09:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: upload the keys of a reused link

hostapd sets the group key of an AP before it starts the AP.  The link has
no channel context at that point, so mt7996_set_hw_key() skips the key and
mt7996_vif_link_add() uploads it when the channel context is assigned.

A link that already exists goes through mt7996_vif_link_reuse() instead,
which uploads no keys.  This is the case for an AP on a DFS channel: the
CAC sets up the link, and the link stays valid when the channel context is
released at the end of the CAC.  mac80211 considers the group key uploaded,
but the firmware has no group key and no cipher for the BSS.

A 4-way handshake hides this, because hostapd sets the group key again for
the first station, now with a channel context.  A station that arrives by
FT has no handshake.  Until another station has completed one, it stays
associated but does not get the data frames sent to it.

Upload the keys in mt7996_vif_link_reuse() as well.

Fixes: e995f6198d8b ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: fix key add/remove imbalance")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -380,6 +380,10 @@ static int mt7996_vif_link_reuse(struct
 				 struct mt7996_vif_link *link)
 {
 	struct mt76_vif_link *mlink = &link->mt76;
+	struct mt7996_key_iter_data it = {
+		.cmd = SET_KEY,
+		.link_id = link_conf->link_id,
+	};
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = mt7996_mcu_add_dev_info(phy, vif, link_conf, mlink, true);
@@ -387,10 +391,17 @@ static int mt7996_vif_link_reuse(struct
 		return ret;
 
 	if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP && ieee80211_vif_is_mld(vif))
-		return mt7996_mcu_mld_link_oper(phy->dev, link_conf, link, true);
+		ret = mt7996_mcu_mld_link_oper(phy->dev, link_conf, link, true);
+	else
+		ret = mt7996_mcu_add_bss_info(phy, vif, link_conf, mlink,
+					      &link->msta_link, true);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/* keys set while the link had no channel context were not uploaded */
+	ieee80211_iter_keys(phy->mt76->hw, vif, mt7996_key_iter, &it);
 
-	return mt7996_mcu_add_bss_info(phy, vif, link_conf, mlink,
-				       &link->msta_link, true);
+	return 0;
 }
 
 int mt7996_vif_link_add(struct mt76_phy *mphy, struct ieee80211_vif *vif,
